{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775350210-w7FfCFUCNdGplpkyHtGq","role":"assistant","created":1775350219,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking about the growth in Employment and General Retirement net budget receipts between two budget proposal releases - FY2013 and FY2023. \n\nLooking at the data, I see:\n- FY2013 budget proposal would typically be released in February 2012 (the President's budget for FY2013)\n- FY2023 budget proposal would typically be released in March 2022 (the President's budget for FY2023)\n\nWait, I need to reconsider this. The FY (fiscal year) budget proposal is usually released in February of the preceding year. For example:\n- FY2013 budget was proposed in February 2012\n- FY2023 budget was proposed in March 2022\n\nBut looking at the data I have - these are Treasury Bulletins from June 2012 and June 2022. The pages I've seen show data for January, February, and March - the second quarter.\n\nLet me reconsider the question - it's asking about the month the budget proposal was released. Looking at historical budget release dates:\n- FY2013 budget proposal was released in February 2012\n- FY2023 budget proposal was released in March 2022 (actually typically it's February, but let me verify)\n\nActually, the President's Budget is typically released in February. But for FY2023, the budget was released in March 2022 because of certain circumstances.\n\nNow, from the data in the treasury bulletins:\n- The 2012 bulletin (for FY2012) shows data for Jan, Feb, Mar 2012 - the second quarter of FY2012\n- The 2022 bulletin (for FY2022) shows data for Jan, Feb, Mar 2022 - the second quarter of FY2022\n\nBut wait - I need the months when the budget proposals were released, not necessarily the data months in the bulletins. Let me think about this again:\n\nFY2013 budget proposal - typically released February 2012\n\n\nFY2023 budget proposal - typically released March 2022\n\nI'll carefully match the data to the correct months. The 2012 bulletin covers the second quarter of FY2012, but for the FY2013 budget proposal, I'd use February 2012 data. Similarly, for the FY2023 proposal, I'd use March 2022 data.\n\nI'll cross-reference the Employment and General Retirement net budget receipts for these specific months to calculate the growth between the two periods.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_1ed19a3bf13783d8","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"cat /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2012_06.json | head -c 5000"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
