{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775350255-r5xEYX4uK3av8yBbrtow","role":"assistant","created":1775350263,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The answer file shows \"73%\". Let me verify my calculation one more time:\n\nFY2013 budget proposal was released in February 2012 (the month the FY2013 budget proposal would have been released is February 2012 - this is the \"month of release\")\n\nFY2023 budget proposal was supposed to be released in February 2022 (the month it was supposed to be released)\n\nEmployment and General Retirement net budget receipts:\n- February 2012: 60.6 billion dollars\n- February 2022: 104.6 billion dollars\n\nPercentage growth = ((104.6 - 60.6) / 60.6) * 100 = (44 / 60.6) * 100 = 72.61%\n\nRounded to nearest whole number = 73%\n\nWait, but there's something subtle here. The FY2013 budget proposal was released in February 2012. But fiscal year 2013 runs from October 2012 to September 2013. So when we talk about the \"month that the FY2013 budget proposal was released,\" this would be February 2012.\n\nSimilarly, the FY2023 budget proposal was released in February 2022 (it's supposed to be released in that month for fiscal year 2023, which runs from October 2022 to September 2023).\n\nSo my interpretation seems correct, and 73% is the answer.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_214aae28cb1d86d2","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"todo__todo_write","arguments":{"content":"- [x] Identify when FY2013 budget proposal was released (month) - February\n- [x] Identify when FY2023 budget proposal was supposed to be released (month) - February\n- [x] Find Employment and General Retirement net budget receipts for those months\n- [x] Calculate percentage growth between the two months\n- [x] Write final answer to /app/answer.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"todo"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
